6. Traditional Programming vs AI/ML
This is a very important distinction.
Traditional programming
Humans explicitly write rules.
DATA + RULES
     │
     ▼
   PROGRAM
     │
     ▼
   OUTPUT

Example:
if marks >= 40:
    print("Pass")
else:
    print("Fail")

The programmer already knows the rule.
7. Machine Learning approach
In ML, we often provide examples and expected outputs during training.
        DATA
          +
   CORRECT ANSWERS
          │
          ▼
    ML ALGORITHM
          │
          ▼
       MODEL

The trained model can then process new data:
New Data
   │
   ▼
Trained Model
   │
   ▼
Prediction

Example: Spam Detection
Training data:
Email	Label
"Win money now"	Spam
"Project meeting tomorrow"	Not Spam
"Claim your free prize"	Spam
"College timetable attached"	Not Spam


The model learns statistical patterns from many examples.
Then:
New Email
    ↓
Trained Model
    ↓
Spam probability
    ↓
Classification

